Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "humans",
	title = "Humans",
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Humans are the most numerous of the younger peoples of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}. They are short-lived beside elves and dwarves, but restless, stubborn and quick to learn. From their bloodlines rose the great kingdoms of the north and south, and from their ranks came the paladins of the {link:holy-light}Holy Light{/link} and the magi of {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}. They have suffered more in the wars against the orcs and the undead than any other people, and they have not yet broken.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[In ancient days the humans lived as scattered tribes in the north, each distrustful of the rest. The {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi{/link} tribe alone saw that the {link:trolls}troll{/link} empire of the Amani would destroy them one by one. Their warlord {link:thoradin}Thoradin{/link} bound the tribes together by strength and by persuasion, and upon their union he founded the nation of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} and its fortress city of {link:stromgarde-keep}Strom{/link}. When the Amani came against the {link:high-elves}high elves{/link} of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}, Arathor answered the elves' call. The elves taught a hundred humans the ways of {link:arcane-magic}arcane magic{/link}, and together the two peoples broke the Amani in the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link}.

In the long peace that followed, the unity of Arathor faded. Its people spread across the land and founded new realms: {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} in the north, {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link} and {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link} on the western shores, {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link} and Stromgarde in the mountains, the city of magi at {link:dalaran}Dalaran{/link}, and in the far south the kingdom of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}, which men now call the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[Humans are a people of kings and of farmers. Their nobles keep old houses and older quarrels, and their commoners work the land with little thought of either. The church of the {link:holy-light}Holy Light{/link} binds many of them together, and its priests are found in every village. Humans value oaths, courage and duty, though they do not always keep to them. Their greatest gift is that they rebuild. Whatever is burned, they raise again.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The human kingdoms are shadows of their former glory. The {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} holds the ruins of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, and the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link} wages its own merciless war in the north. {link:gilneas}Gilneas{/link} has shut itself behind its great wall. {link:alterac-mountains}Alterac{/link} is ruined, and {link:stromgarde-keep}Stromgarde{/link} clings to what remains of the {link:arathi-highlands}Arathi Highlands{/link}. In the south, {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} stands rebuilt, but King {link:varian-wrynn}Varian Wrynn{/link} has vanished, and Highlord {link:bolvar-fordragon}Bolvar Fordragon{/link} rules in his name. Across the sea, Lady {link:jaina-proudmoore}Jaina Proudmoore{/link} keeps the island fortress of {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}, where humans hold an uneasy peace with the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. Humanity remains the heart of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}, and it is a heart that bleeds.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "dwarves",
	title = "Dwarves",
	aliases = { "dwarf" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The dwarves are a stout and hardy people of the mountains of Khaz Modan. They are miners, smiths, brewers and warriors, and they are among the finest craftsmen in the world. Their great city of {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link} is carved into the heart of a mountain. They have fought beside humankind since the {link:second-war}Second War{/link}, and they remain one of the pillars of the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[For ages the dwarves lived beneath the mountains, and their own legends said they were shaped from stone. In the halls of {link:uldaman}Uldaman{/link}, scholars of the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} have found records of the titans that seem to bear this out: they speak of the earthen, beings of living rock made by the titans to shape the deep places of the world. Many dwarves now believe that their people descend from them.

The dwarves were long united under one high king in {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}. When that king died, three great clans went to war for his throne. In this War of the Three Hammers the Bronzebeard clan held Ironforge. The Wildhammer clan was driven north and in time made its home in the {link:the-hinterlands}Hinterlands{/link}. The {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Iron clan{/link} was cast into the south. There its sorcerer-king, {link:ruins-of-thaurissan}Thaurissan{/link}, sought a power to avenge his defeat, and he called up {red:ragnaros}Ragnaros{/red} the Firelord. The fire of that summoning broke the land and bound the Dark Irons to the Firelord's service.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[Dwarves are proud, loyal and slow to forgive. They love good ale, loud song and a well-made axe. They respect deeds more than words and are known for their long memories. Their gunsmiths are famed across the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}, and their rifles and cannon have held many walls. The Wildhammers are wilder than their kin and ride gryphons into battle, while the Bronzebeards prefer the forge and the rifle.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[King {link:magni-bronzebeard}Magni Bronzebeard{/link} rules in {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}. His brother {link:brann-bronzebeard}Brann Bronzebeard{/link} leads the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link}, whose delvers dig through ruins across the world in search of the dwarves' true past. Ironforge has opened its gates to the {link:gnomes}gnomes{/link} who lost their city to the {link:troggs}troggs{/link}, and {link:tinker-town}Tinker Town{/link} now rings with gnomish work. The {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Iron Dwarves{/link} remain the bitterest foes of their cousins, and in the depths of {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link} they labor in the service of the Firelord. The Wildhammers keep their own counsel in the {link:the-hinterlands}Hinterlands{/link}, allies of Ironforge but never its subjects.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "gnomes",
	title = "Gnomes",
	aliases = { "gnome" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The gnomes are a small, clever and endlessly curious people. They are the greatest tinkers and engineers in the world, and they see a problem to be solved in everything they meet. For generations they lived in the wondrous city of {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} in the mountains of {link:dun-morogh}Dun Morogh{/link}. That city is lost to them now, and they live as guests of the {link:dwarves}dwarves{/link} in {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The gnomes have long been neighbors and friends of the dwarves of Khaz Modan. Of their earliest days, the histories of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} say little. What is certain is that they built {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link} with their own hands and filled it with marvels: great engines, clockwork servants and devices that no other people could have imagined. In the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} they joined the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} beside the dwarves. They sent few soldiers, for they are not a numerous people, but they gave the Alliance flying machines, submarines and weapons of their own design.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[Gnomes are bright, quick and cheerful even in the darkest hours. They are also easily distracted, and their inventions do not always do what their makers intended. They prize cleverness above strength, and they hold their master engineers in the highest honor. Their leader bears the title of High Tinker. Many gnomes also study {link:arcane-magic}arcane magic{/link}, and some turn to darker arts that others think best left alone.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[After the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, the {link:troggs}troggs{/link} rose from beneath the earth and poured into {link:gnomeregan}Gnomeregan{/link}. The city could not be held. High Tinker {link:gelbin-mekkatorque}Gelbin Mekkatorque{/link} made a desperate choice and unleashed a toxic weapon to drive out the invaders. It slew many troggs, but it also slew a great many gnomes, and it left the city poisoned. The survivors fled to {link:ironforge}Ironforge{/link}. It is now whispered that the fall was no accident: the High Tinker's own advisor, {link:mekgineer-thermaplugg}Sicco Thermaplugg{/link}, is said to have betrayed his people, and he now rules the ruined city as its mad master. The gnomes dream of the day they will take their home back. Until then, they tinker in Ironforge and serve the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} with the same zeal they have always shown.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "night-elves",
	title = "Night Elves",
	aliases = { "kaldorei", "kal'dorei", "night elf" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The night elves, who call themselves the kaldorei or "children of the stars", are the oldest civilized people of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. They are tall, violet-skinned and long-lived, and they have guarded the forests of the north for ten thousand years. Their priestesses serve the moon goddess Elune, and their druids tend the wild in the ways taught by the demigod {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link}. After the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, they joined the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} for the first time in their history.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The first night elves were a tribe that settled on the shores of the {link:well-of-eternity}Well of Eternity{/link} in ancient times. The Well's power changed them and gave them long life. On its shores they raised a great empire, ruled by {link:queen-azshara}Queen Azshara{/link} and her caste of Highborne sorcerers. The Highborne grew drunk on the Well's power, and at last their magic drew the eye of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. {link:azshara}Azshara{/link} opened the way for the demons, and the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link} began.

The druid {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion Stormrage{/link}, the priestess {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande Whisperwind{/link} and their allies drove the Legion back. In the end the Well was destroyed, and the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link} shattered the ancient continent. The night elves who survived turned away from arcane magic. On {link:mount-hyjal}Mount Hyjal{/link} they tended a new tree of life, {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link}, which granted them immortality. The Highborne who refused to give up their magic were sent into exile across the sea.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[The night elves are a patient and watchful people. Their women have long served as the {link:sentinels}Sentinels{/link}, the warriors who guard the forests, while their men became druids who slept for long years in the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link}. They love the wild places of the world and hate those who despoil them. They do not trust the arcane, for it nearly ended their world.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, the Legion returned. At the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, the night elves, humans and orcs stood together against {link:archimonde}Archimonde{/link}, and {link:nordrassil}Nordrassil{/link}'s power was spent to destroy him. With it, the night elves lost their immortality. Archdruid {link:fandral-staghelm}Fandral Staghelm{/link} and his druids then raised a new World Tree, {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link}, off the northern coast, and the city of {link:darnassus}Darnassus{/link} grew in its boughs. {link:tyrande-whisperwind}Tyrande{/link} rules there as High Priestess, while {link:malfurion-stormrage}Malfurion{/link} walks the {link:emerald-dream}Emerald Dream{/link} and has not returned. The kaldorei now face the orcs who cut the forests of {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link}, and the corruption that spreads through {link:felwood}Felwood{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "orcs",
	title = "Orcs",
	aliases = { "orc" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The orcs are a proud warrior people from the world of Draenor. They came to {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} as conquerors through the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}, and they brought fire and ruin to the human kingdoms. They were defeated, imprisoned and broken, yet they rose again. Under their Warchief {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} they have crossed the sea to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} and built a new homeland in {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}. They are the heart of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[On Draenor the orcs lived as many clans. They were hunters and warriors, guided by shamans who spoke with the spirits of the {link:elements}elements{/link}. The demon lord {link:kil-jaeden}Kil'jaeden{/link} set out to make them into a weapon of the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}. He deceived the elder shaman {link:ner-zhul}Ner'zhul{/link}, and after him Ner'zhul's apprentice {link:gul-dan}Gul'dan{/link}. Gul'dan taught the clans the warlock's arts, and the elements turned away from the orcs. At last the chieftains drank the blood of the demon {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link}, and a bloodlust took hold of the whole people.

Through the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link} the {link:horde}Horde{/link} fell upon the kingdom of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. It won the {link:first-war}First War{/link} and burned {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}. Under {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link} it nearly won the {link:second-war}Second War{/link} as well, but it was betrayed from within and defeated. The surviving orcs were herded into internment camps, where a strange lethargy settled over them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[The orcs honor strength, courage and loyalty to the clan. They respect the shaman who speaks for the spirits and the warrior who stands firm in battle. Their names are proud, and so is their memory: each clan keeps its own legends and its own grudges. Since the end of the demon's curse, many orcs have returned to the old ways of the shaman and seek balance with the elements.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The young orc {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}, raised as a slave in a human fortress, escaped his masters and freed his people from the camps. At the call of a prophet he led them west to {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. There, in the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, {link:grom-hellscream}Grom Hellscream{/link} slew {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link} and freed the orcs from the demon's blood. Thrall named his new land {link:durotar}Durotar{/link} after his father, Durotan, and his capital {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link} after Doomhammer. The orcs now hold an uneasy peace with {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}. Yet not all orcs have turned from the old darkness. The cult of the {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link} whispers in the caves of Durotar, and in the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link} the {link:blackrock-clan}Blackrock clan{/link} still serves the black dragons in {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "trolls",
	title = "Trolls",
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The trolls are among the most ancient peoples of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. They are tall, tusked and fierce, and their bodies heal wounds that would kill any other creature. Long before the night elves raised their empire, the trolls ruled great realms of their own. Those empires have fallen, and the tribes that remain are bitter, divided and dangerous. One of them, the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} tribe, now stands with the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The oldest troll kingdom was that of the Zandalari, whose tribe dwelt far to the south. From them came the two great empires of ancient times: the Amani in the northern forests and the Gurubashi in the southern jungles. They worshipped powerful spirits called the loa, and they warred with the early night elves and lost. The {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link} tore their lands apart.

The Amani never forgave the high elves who settled in their forests. In the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link} they came close to destroying {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}, until the humans of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} joined the elves and broke them. In the south, the Gurubashi fell into civil war when the priests of the Atal'ai called up {link:hakkar}Hakkar{/link}, the blood god. The tribes cast the god down and drove the Atal'ai into the swamps, where they built the temple of {link:temple-of-atal-hakkar}Atal'Hakkar{/link}. Their empire never recovered.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[Trolls are hunters and raiders. Their priests practice voodoo and speak with the loa, and their witch doctors brew potions and hexes that other peoples fear. Many tribes hold to cruel customs, and some are said to eat their foes. They are proud of their ancient past and resentful of the younger peoples who took their lands. Few trolls trust outsiders, and fewer still are trusted in return.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear tribe{/link} was driven from its home in the jungles and found refuge in the southern seas. There {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} saved them from the humans and the sea witch, and their leader Sen'jin gave his life so that his people might follow the orcs. Today the Darkspears serve the {link:horde}Horde{/link} under {link:vol-jin}Vol'jin{/link}. They settled the {link:echo-isles}Echo Isles{/link} off {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}, but a witch doctor named {link:zalazane}Zalazane{/link} has seized the islands with dark magic, and the tribe has withdrawn to {link:sen-jin-village}Sen'jin Village{/link} on the mainland. Elsewhere the troll tribes remain enemies of all: the Amani in the northern forests, the {link:witherbark-trolls}Witherbark{/link} and Vilebranch in the {link:the-hinterlands}Hinterlands{/link}, the Gurubashi tribes of {link:stranglethorn-vale}Stranglethorn Vale{/link}, the {link:sandfury-trolls}Sandfury{/link} of {link:tanaris}Tanaris{/link} and the {link:frostmane-trolls}Frostmane{/link} of {link:dun-morogh}Dun Morogh{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "tauren",
	title = "Tauren",
	aliases = { "tauren", "shu'halo" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The tauren are a people of great stature and gentle wisdom who roam the plains of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. They are huge and bull-like, and they can be terrible in battle, but they would rather live in peace with the land. They revere the Earth Mother above all things. Under their great chieftain {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link} they have settled the grasslands of {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link} and joined the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The tauren, who call themselves the shu'halo, are among the oldest peoples of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. For ages they wandered the plains as nomads, following the great herds and the turning of the seasons. They say that the Earth Mother gave them the land, and that the sun and the moon are her eyes, which they name An'she and Mu'sha. The tribes lived apart, each with its own chieftains and its own totems.

That life was nearly ended by the {link:centaurs}centaur{/link}. The cruel horse-men of the plains hunted the scattered tribes for generations and drove them from their ancestral lands. {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne Bloodhoof{/link} set himself to unite the tribes against them. When the orcs came to Kalimdor, Cairne met the young {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}, and the two peoples recognized each other as kin in spirit. With the help of the orcs the tauren broke the centaur's hold on {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link} and claimed it as their homeland.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[The tauren live close to the land. They hunt with respect and take only what they need. Their shamans speak with the spirits of the {link:elements}elements{/link} and of their ancestors, and some tauren have learned the ways of the druid, trained by the night elves of the {link:cenarion-circle}Cenarion Circle{/link}. They are patient, slow to anger and honest to a fault. Their totems record the lineages and the deeds of their tribes.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The tauren have built their capital of {link:thunder-bluff}Thunder Bluff{/link} on high mesas above {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link}, reached by great lifts. {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne{/link} rules there as High Chieftain, respected even by those who fear the {link:horde}Horde{/link}. Not all the tribes share his vision. The {link:grimtotem-clan}Grimtotem tribe{/link}, led by the elder crone {link:magatha-grimtotem}Magatha{/link}, keeps its own ambitions, and many in Thunder Bluff trust it little. Around Mulgore the tauren still face enemies: the {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} of the {link:bristleback-quilboar}Bristleback{/link} tribe, the harpies of the ridges and the {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} of {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}. The tauren honor their debt to the orcs, and they are among the Horde's most steadfast members.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "forsaken",
	title = "Forsaken",
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Forsaken are undead who have broken free of the will of the Lich King. Once they were the people of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}. They died in the plague, rose as slaves of the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}, and then, in a single hour of weakness in their master's grip, woke to their own minds again. They follow {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link}, the Banshee Queen, and they have made a dark kingdom beneath the ruins of their old capital. For reasons of their own, they have joined the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, the plague of the {link:cult-of-the-damned}Cult of the Damned{/link} swept across {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, and Prince {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} murdered his father {link:terenas-menethil}Terenas Menethil{/link} and gave the kingdom to the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}. Thousands who died rose again in the service of the Lich King. For a time they had no will at all.

Then the Lich King's power faltered, and many of the undead in Lordaeron found that they could think for themselves once more. {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link}, the fallen ranger-general of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}, had been raised as a banshee by Arthas himself. She broke free with them. She turned against the dreadlords who sought to rule the ruined kingdom, and she bound one of them, {link:varimathras}Varimathras{/link}, to her service. She named her people the Forsaken, and she led them to take the ruins of Lordaeron's capital as their own.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[The Forsaken remember their lives, but they cannot return to them. Their friends and kin fear and hate them, and many of them have learned to hate in return. They are grim, bitter and practical. Their scholars pursue every art of alchemy and necromancy without shame, and their priests have turned from the {link:holy-light}Holy Light{/link} to the shadow. Among the living they are tolerated rather than trusted.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Beneath the shattered city of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} the Forsaken have raised the {link:undercity}Undercity{/link}, a maze of halls and sewers built in the old royal crypts. From there {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas{/link} rules {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal Glades{/link} and wages war on two fronts: against the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} that still holds the plaguelands, and against the {link:scarlet-crusade}Scarlet Crusade{/link}, which burns every undead it finds. Their alliance with the {link:horde}Horde{/link} is one of need. The orcs and {link:tauren}tauren{/link} find them strange and unsettling. The Forsaken, for their part, say little of their true aims, and the chemists of the {link:royal-apothecary-society}Royal Apothecary Society{/link} labor in secret on a new plague.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "skyborne",
	title = "Skyborne",
	aliases = { "shen'dorei" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Skyborne, who call themselves the shen'dorei or "hidden people", are elves who have lived for thousands of years beyond the world itself. Their home is {link:zephras-isle}Zephras Isle{/link}, an island that floats in {link:skywall}Skywall{/link}, the elemental plane of air. They share the blood of the Highborne, and they are cousins of the {link:high-elves}high elves{/link} of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}. Now their sky-borne realm is failing, and a new generation of Skyborne has come down to {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link} in search of answers.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The Skyborne trace their line to the Highborne of Eldre'Thalas, the city in {link:feralas}Feralas{/link} now called {red:dire-maul}Dire Maul{/red}. After the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}, Prince {red:tortheldrin}Tortheldrin{/red} sought to sustain the city with ever more dangerous powers. Some of his people had seen what such hunger for power had done to the world, and they rose against him. They thwarted his designs, but their rebellion was crushed, and they fled across the sea with the prince's fleet close behind them.

Far to the west, they came upon a land ruled by ancient spirits of the {link:elements}elements{/link}. There they made a pact with the spirits of the wind. The spirits tore a great part of that land into the sky and carried it out of the world, and they anchored it in {link:skywall}Skywall{/link}. Hidden from their pursuers, the exiles built a small and bright civilization among the clouds.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[The long ages in {link:skywall}Skywall{/link} changed the shen'dorei. They grew lighter and swifter than their ancestors, and the magic of the air marked their hair, their eyes and their skin. They lived beside the {link:vanishing-of-the-wind-spirits}wind spirits{/link} as students and friends. Some among them received the spirits' gift of skysight, the power to see across the elemental plane. The spirits rarely spoke of {link:al-akir}Al'Akir{/link} the Windlord, master of Skywall, and among the Skyborne his name became a thing of dread and silence.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Without warning, the {link:vanishing-of-the-wind-spirits}wind spirits{/link} vanished. The ancient pylons that hold {link:zephras-isle}Zephras Isle{/link} together have begun to fail, parts of the island have fallen into ruin, and its communities are cut off from one another. The Skyborne are divided over what to do.

• {b}The {link:windshapers}Windshapers{/link}.{/b} Descended from the first shen'dorei to receive skysight, they are the spiritual guides of the island. They seek to learn what became of the wind spirits and to restore them. They have joined the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.
• {b}The {link:high-order}High Order{/link}.{/b} Descended from the Highborne magisters who fled Eldre'Thalas, they believe that the Skyborne trusted their patrons too much. They seek the arcane knowledge their ancestors lost, so that their people may stand on their own. They have joined the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link}.
• {b}The {link:al-aketh}Al'Aketh{/link}.{/b} A cult that turned from the rest of the shen'dorei to serve {link:al-akir}Al'Akir{/link}. Emboldened by the spirits' absence, they have spread fear and seized much of the island.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "high-elves",
	title = "High Elves",
	aliases = { "quel'dorei", "high elf" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The high elves, or quel'dorei, are the children of the Highborne exiles who crossed the sea after the {link:great-sundering}Great Sundering{/link}. In the forests of northern {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link} they built the kingdom of {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link} and its shining capital, Silvermoon. For thousands of years they were the masters of {link:arcane-magic}arcane magic{/link} in the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link}. In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, their kingdom was nearly destroyed.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[After the {link:great-sundering}Sundering{/link}, the night elves forbade the use of arcane magic. The Highborne who would not obey, led by {red:dath-remar-sunstrider}Dath'Remar Sunstrider{/red}, were exiled. They sailed east and after long wandering came to the northern forests, where they fought the Amani {link:trolls}trolls{/link} for their new home. There they created the Sunwell, a fount of arcane power that sustained their people. When the Amani rose against them, they allied with the {link:humans}humans{/link} of {link:arathor}Arathor{/link} and taught them magic, and together they won the {link:troll-wars}Troll Wars{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[The high elves are graceful, proud and learned. They love beauty and magic, and many of them look down upon the younger peoples. Their rangers are the finest archers of the north. Their bond with the Sunwell ran so deep that they came to depend on its power.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[In the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, {link:arthas-menethil}Arthas Menethil{/link} led the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link} into {link:quel-thalas}Quel'Thalas{/link}. He slew King Anasterian Sunstrider and used the Sunwell to raise the lich {link:kel-thuzad}Kel'Thuzad{/link}. Ranger-General {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link} fell in the defense of her homeland. The few who survived remain scattered: some still hold what is left of Quel'Thalas, some serve the {link:alliance}Alliance{/link} and the {link:kirin-tor}Kirin Tor{/link}, and a small band keeps the hunting lodge of {link:quel-danil-lodge}Quel'Danil{/link} in the {link:the-hinterlands}Hinterlands{/link}. Prince Kael'thas, the heir of the Sunstriders, gathered many of the survivors and renamed them the sin'dorei, the blood elves, in memory of the fallen. What has become of him since, no chronicle of these lands can say.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "kobolds",
	title = "Kobolds",
	aliases = { "kobold" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Kobolds are small, rat-like creatures who dwell in mines and caverns across {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. They are cowardly, greedy and not very clever, but there are a great many of them. Wherever an old mine is left unguarded, the kobolds move in. Each wears a candle upon its head to light the tunnels, and each would sooner die than give it up.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records where the kobolds first came from. Some delvers of the {link:explorers-league}Explorers' League{/link} believe that they arose from the {link:troggs}troggs{/link} of the deep places. Whatever their beginnings, they were already a nuisance to the first settlers of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal{/link}, and they have plagued miners ever since.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[Kobolds love the dark tunnels but fear the true dark, and their candles are the most precious things they own. To steal one is the worst of crimes, and the thief will hear about it. They dig endlessly and hoard whatever glitters. Their geomancers work crude magic of fire and stone. Most are content to fight only when cornered, but in a swarm they can overwhelm a careless miner.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Kobolds infest the mines of {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn Forest{/link} and {link:westfall}Westfall{/link}, where they dig for gold that does not stay in their hands. It is said that they are driven by the {link:riverpaw-gnolls}Riverpaw gnolls{/link}, who in turn deal with the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link}. The {link:tunnel-rat-kobolds}Tunnel Rats{/link} trouble the dwarves of {link:loch-modan}Loch Modan{/link}, and in {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} kobolds dig for the {link:venture-company}Venture Company{/link} in the {link:stonetalon-mountains}Stonetalon Mountains{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "gnolls",
	title = "Gnolls",
	aliases = { "gnoll" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Gnolls are hyena-like creatures who roam the wild places of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link} and {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. They are brutish, quarrelsome and hungry, and they value strength above all else. They live in packs and clans, each ruled by the strongest among them, and they raid the farms and roads of other peoples for food and plunder.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The gnolls are an old people of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}, and no chronicle records their beginnings. They were among the dangers faced by the first human settlers in the north. The kingdom of {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} remembers a darker time, when a packlord of the {link:redridge-gnolls}Redridge gnolls{/link} named Garfang gathered the clans into a great host and struck at the kingdom's farms. King Barathen Wrynn rode out and slew him, and the packs tore themselves apart in the struggle that followed.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[Gnolls prefer to let others do their work. Their leaders drive the weak before them, and they gladly serve any stronger master who promises them food and loot. Their mystics practice a crude shamanism. They are cunning enough to set traps and ambushes, and cruel enough to enjoy them.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[Gnolls trouble nearly every border of the human lands. The {link:riverpaw-gnolls}Riverpaw{/link} raid {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn Forest{/link} and {link:westfall}Westfall{/link}. The {link:redridge-gnolls}Redridge pack{/link} and the {link:shadowhide-gnolls}Shadowhide{/link} prowl the {link:redridge-mountains}Redridge Mountains{/link}, the latter in thrall to the warlock {link:morganth}Morganth{/link}. The Mosshide haunt the {link:wetlands}Wetlands{/link}, the Rot Hide dig up the dead of {link:tirisfal-glades}Tirisfal Glades{/link} for the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}, and other clans roam the hills of {link:hillsbrad-foothills}Hillsbrad{/link} and the forests of {link:feralas}Feralas{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "riverpaw-gnolls",
	title = "Riverpaw Gnolls",
	aliases = { "Riverpaw gnolls", "Riverpaw" },
	category = "group",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Riverpaw are the {link:gnolls}gnoll{/link} clan that plagues the southern lands of the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}. They range along the border of {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn Forest{/link}, through the fields of {link:westfall}Westfall{/link} and toward the {link:redridge-mountains}Redridge Mountains{/link}. They raid farms, ambush travellers and fight the few soldiers the kingdom can spare. The most feared of them is the great gnoll {link:hogger}Hogger{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[The Riverpaw have grown bolder since the kingdom's army was sent abroad. They come out of Forest's Edge to strike at the farms of southern {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link}, and {link:westbrook-garrison}Westbrook Garrison{/link} pays a bounty for every paw its volunteers bring back. In {link:westfall}Westfall{/link} their camps are larger still. The People's Militia has found signs that the Riverpaw do not fight for themselves alone: they drive {link:kobolds}kobold{/link} slaves in the mines, and they deal with the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link}. Many in {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} wonder who arms them, and who gives them their unusual cunning.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "murlocs",
	title = "Murlocs",
	aliases = { "murloc" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Murlocs are small, fish-like creatures who live along the coasts, lakes and rivers of {link:azeroth}Azeroth{/link}. They walk on two legs, speak in a gurgling tongue that no other people understands, and attack in sudden swarms. Every fisherman of the {link:eastern-kingdoms}Eastern Kingdoms{/link} and {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} has a tale of the murlocs.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records where the murlocs came from. They have haunted the shores of the world for as long as any people has kept records, and they seem to care nothing for the wars of the land-dwellers.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[Murlocs live in tribes, in villages of huts built along the water's edge. They hunt fish and whatever else strays near their shores. Their oracles and tidehunters wield a simple magic of water and storm. They are rarely dangerous alone, but they seldom come alone. When one murloc is attacked, others appear from the shallows with a terrible cry.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The murlocs have grown bold as the kingdoms weaken. They raid the lakeshores of {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn Forest{/link} and the coast of {link:westfall}Westfall{/link}. The Bluegill tribe haunts the marshes of the {link:wetlands}Wetlands{/link}, and the Greymist tribe the shores of {link:darkshore}Darkshore{/link}. On every coast, from {link:stranglethorn-vale}Stranglethorn Vale{/link} to {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}, their huts stand at the water's edge.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "quilboar",
	title = "Quilboar",
	aliases = { "quilboar" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The quilboar are a savage people of boar-men who dwell in the southern {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link} and the lands around it. They are covered in bristles and thorns, and they make their homes among great tangled thorn vines. They are hostile to nearly every other people, and they have long been at war with the {link:tauren}tauren{/link} and the orcs.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The quilboar hold that they are the children of Agamaggan, the great boar demigod. In the {link:war-of-the-ancients}War of the Ancients{/link}, Agamaggan fought against the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} and was slain. Where his blood fell, immense thorn vines grew from the earth. These thorns became the Razorfen, and the quilboar made them their sacred home.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[The quilboar are fierce and territorial. Their tribes are led by warlords, and their geomancers call upon the earth. They revere the memory of Agamaggan and hold the Razorfen holy. Some of their priestesses have turned to darker arts, and some of their warriors to darker masters.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:razormane-quilboar}Razormane tribe{/link} raids the edges of {link:durotar}Durotar{/link} and the northern {link:the-barrens}Barrens{/link}, and the {link:bristleback-quilboar}Bristleback{/link} tribe troubles the plains of {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link}. In the south, the quilboar dwell in the great thorn warrens of {link:razorfen-kraul}Razorfen Kraul{/link} and {link:razorfen-downs}Razorfen Downs{/link}. It is said that in the Downs a cult called the {link:death-s-head}Death's Head{/link} has turned to the {link:scourge}Scourge{/link}, and that a lich now dwells among them.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "centaurs",
	title = "Centaurs",
	aliases = { "centaur" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The centaur are a cruel and warlike people of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. They have the upper body of a man and the body of a horse, and they are terrible raiders who ride in fast, merciless bands. For generations they have been the greatest enemies of the {link:tauren}tauren{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The centaur are said to descend from the union of Zaetar, a son of the demigod {link:cenarius}Cenarius{/link}, and Theradras, a princess of the elemental earth. Their earliest children were cruel beyond measure, and in a fit of jealousy they slew their own father. Theradras laid Zaetar to rest in the caverns of {red:maraudon}Maraudon{/red}, where his spirit is said to linger still.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[The centaur live as nomads and raiders. They hold that the strong should take what they want from the weak. Their khans lead the tribes, and the tribes war among themselves when they have no other foes. They are skilled riders and archers, and they show little mercy.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The {link:kolkar-centaurs}Kolkar tribe{/link} roams {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}, and its raiders strike at the orcish outposts there. The Galak ride through {link:thousand-needles}Thousand Needles{/link}. In {link:desolace}Desolace{/link}, the Magram and the Gelkis wage a long feud, and both claim the favor of Theradras. The Maraudine guard the entrance to Maraudon itself. Though {link:cairne-bloodhoof}Cairne{/link} drove the centaur from {link:mulgore}Mulgore{/link}, they have not forgotten the {link:tauren}tauren{/link}.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
	kind = "topic",
	id = "furbolgs",
	title = "Furbolgs",
	aliases = { "furbolg" },
	category = "people",
	unlock = {
		{ type = "read" },
	},
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Furbolgs are bear-like people of the northern forests of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. They were long a gentle and peaceful folk, friends of the {link:night-elves}night elves{/link} and of the druids. In recent years a sickness of the spirit has fallen upon most of their tribes, and many furbolgs have become savage and hostile.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The furbolgs have lived in the forests of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} since ancient times. They were once counted among the allies of the {link:night-elves}kaldorei{/link}. No chronicle records their beginnings in more detail.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Nature and Customs",
			text = [=[Furbolgs live in tribes, in dens and villages hidden deep in the woods. Their shamans are wise in the ways of the forest. Most were content to live quietly and trade in peace with their neighbors.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "In the Present Day",
			text = [=[The demonic taint left in the forests since the {link:third-war}Third War{/link} has driven many tribes mad. The {link:thistlefur-village}Thistlefur{/link} and Foulweald of {link:ashenvale}Ashenvale{/link}, the {link:deadwood-furbolgs}Deadwood{/link} of {link:felwood}Felwood{/link}, the {link:blackwood-furbolgs}Blackwood{/link} of {link:darkshore}Darkshore{/link}, the {link:gnarlpine-furbolgs}Gnarlpine{/link} of {link:teldrassil}Teldrassil{/link} and the {link:winterfall-furbolgs}Winterfall{/link} of {link:winterspring}Winterspring{/link} have turned against their old friends. Only the {link:timbermaw-furbolgs}Timbermaw{/link} have held out against the corruption. They guard the passes of {link:timbermaw-hold}Timbermaw Hold{/link} and trust no outsider until they have proven themselves.]=],
		},
	},
})

Add({
